# Gmail AI Filter with n8n and HuggingFace

This project is an automated email processing workflow built using **n8n**, designed to read new emails from **Gmail**, analyze their importance using **HuggingFace's NLP model**, and store only the important ones into a **Google Sheets** document.

### 🔍 How It Works
1. **Gmail Trigger**: Watches for new incoming emails.
2. **HuggingFace Integration**: Sends the email content (snippet) to `facebook/bart-large-mnli` model to classify whether it's "important" or "not important".
3. **IF Node**: Checks if the classification result is "important".
4. **Google Sheets**: Appends or updates the important email (ID, snippet, date) into a selected Google Sheet.

### ✅ Technologies Used
- [n8n](https://n8n.io) – open-source workflow automation tool
- [HuggingFace Inference API](https://huggingface.co/inference-api) – for zero-shot text classification
- [Google Sheets API](https://developers.google.com/sheets/api) – for storing structured email data
- [Gmail API](https://developers.google.com/gmail/api) – for reading incoming messages

### 📄 File Structure
- `gmail-ai-to-sheets.json`: n8n workflow export file

### 🚀 Use Case
This setup is useful for:
- Filtering important emails automatically
- Tracking job-related or urgent messages
- Creating a smart email log for analysis or review

